{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>My statutes you shall keep.</b> The verse circles back: above He warned concerning the statutes of forbidden relations, and here He warns concerning the statutes of mixed species, to teach you that one may not graft a fruit tree onto another fruit tree." "<b>Your animal you shall not mate as mixed species.</b> After commanding to be holy, not to do wrong to one's fellow, He likewise commanded not to do so to an animal, and regarding other matters — not to alter in them the act of HaShem. For just as HaShem commanded in the act of Creation that each and every one bring forth fruit למינהו (after its kind), so too He commanded and warned concerning all matters of mixed species." "<b>And a garment of mixed species.</b> One may say the reason they are forbidden is because the priestly garments were of wool and linen, as is said in the relevant passage: 'he felt the tunic of tekhelet — it was wool,' like the fat and blood and the anointing oil and the incense, which are forbidden — for it would be like one using the scepter of the king."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:31.702269933Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}